    <briefdescription>
<para>Foster 1992 probability of collision algorithm as described in: </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Foster, J.L., Estes, H.S. (1992). A Parametric Analysis of Orbital Debris Collision Probability and Maneuver Rate for Space Vehicles. NASA/JSC-25898.</para>
<para>The two-dimensional probability density function of the relative position is integrated over the combined hard-body circle in the encounter plane, in polar coordinates centered on the hard-body circle, as described in Equation 2 of:</para>
<para>Alfano, Salvatore. (2007). Review of Conjunction Probability Methods for Short-term Encounters. AAS 07-148.</para>
<para>The hard-body circle is sectioned into radial steps (annular sectors) and angular slices, and the probability density function is evaluated at the center of each resulting cell (midpoint rule).</para>
<para>The algorithm relies on the following assumptions:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>High relative speed encounter </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
